const helperBytes = fs.readFileSync(path.join(plan, 'proposed', helperTarget));
const helper = save('after/' + helperTarget + '.snapshot', helperBytes, 'work/bsdtar-oracle-hosted-plan-20261015/proposed/' + helperTarget);
transitions.push({ target: helperTarget, before: null, after: { sourcePath: helper.path, ...identity(helperBytes) }, adaptations: [] });
save('README.txt', Buffer.from(`Hosted bsdtar oracle-test overlay: SOURCE ONLY, unexecuted.\n\nThis inert bundle preserves the exact work-only plan, independent acquisition-source review, two patches, two unchanged test before-images, their narrowly authored after-images, and the exact proposed helper. Active application files are unchanged. The helper authenticates and copies the EXE plus its paired archiveint.dll only inside existing private test fixtures. The two test bodies, banner assertions, fixtures and expected outcomes are retained.\n\nA future hosted composer may change only formats.test.mjs, zstd.test.mjs and the new bsdtar-original-test-helper.mjs in an ephemeral clean checkout. Its source identity combines the actual baseline Git commit and the composition receipt. Composer acquisition/original/test executions remain zero. Bootstrap, paired-loader execution, comparisons and full-suite acceptance require distinct actual hosted evidence.\n\nThe EXE pin equals the historical pin. The newly explicit paired-build DLL pin does not establish which DLL the earlier EXE-only historical run loaded. Historical receipts and snapshots retain their original attribution. No vendor image is included in this bundle.\n`), 'new source-only bundle description');
