from pathlib import Path
import hashlib, json, difflib

ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
REPO=ROOT/'outputs/rea-research-lab'
STAGE=ROOT/'work/d24-failure-current-docs-20261016-next'
assert not STAGE.exists(), 'Preserve existing stages; choose a new version'
paths=['README.md','CLOUD-VERIFICATION.md','products/rea-studio/STATUS.json']
before={p:(REPO/p).read_bytes() for p in paths}
ident=lambda b:{'bytes':len(b),'sha256':hashlib.sha256(b).hexdigest()}
failure='products/rea-studio/results/cloud-full1100-native-metadata-failure-20261016/preservation-manifest.json'
intro=(
"The latest hosted full-suite repeat, [run `38933603615`](https://github.com/Ginderlax/rea-research-lab/actions/runs/38933603615) on the metadata-only branch revision `089cb234`, passes **1,100/1,100 checks with zero failures or skips**. Its complete 431-file local evidence backup is readable. The immediately preceding [D24 full-suite failure]("+failure+") remains unresolved: run `38932318510` passed **1,098 of 1,100 checks** and failed two Archive creation groups when native Windows source metadata was unavailable or invalid. Both failed groups took about 15.6â€“15.8 seconds against a 15-second native-child limit, but the original transport error was redacted, so a timeout is an inference, not an observed cause. A separate hosted diagnostic is being prepared with the same runtime deadline and assertions. The newer pass neither diagnoses nor erases the failed attempt; its exact ZIP, raw output and all 431 uploaded files remain recoverable. Earlier 1,100-pass epochs retain their original source scope.\n\n"
"Committed Notes task editing separately passes **92/92 groups and eight browser scenarios** on its recorded 32-file source epoch. The New To-do **111/111 and eight-scenario** result below remains an experiment; its 36-file source is not installed. Current publication verification passes all **208 controls, both root phases and 963 syntax checks**, with 92 readable artifact files and 56 authenticated Notes-envelope sources. The exact two derived metadata files were imported at `089cb234`; its automatic repeat confirms the same canonical payload and manifest. These later preservation and documentation changes need fresh publication validation. Complete-product parity and superiority remain unproven."
)
readme=before['README.md'].decode('utf-8')
old=next(x for x in readme.splitlines() if x.startswith('The latest [hosted verification]'))
assert readme.count(old)==1
readme=readme.replace(old,intro,1)

cloud=before['CLOUD-VERIFICATION.md'].decode('utf-8')
marker='## Latest verified follow-up\n\n'
if marker not in cloud: marker='## Latest verified follow-up\r\n\r\n'
assert cloud.count(marker)==1
cloud_intro=(
"The latest completed full-suite repeat is [run `38933603615`](https://github.com/Ginderlax/rea-research-lab/actions/runs/38933603615): **1,100/1,100 checks pass**, with zero failures, skips, cancellations or todos, on actual tested merge `ca0de9212406f69dd46f87e499025bb0f001f4a6` for metadata-only branch head `089cb2341cea6519a2bbb11f2c6588131f6e67bd`. All 798 census identities remain stable and all 374 active snapshots are retained in its complete 431-file readable local backup. Artifact `12061336112` is 1,726,276 bytes with SHA256 `8aa4c41f307d77347a015f78a6f7beab29361bb75b6c973b91e87ffe93627947`. This is a separate repeat, not a replacement for any earlier receipt.\n\n"
"The immediately preceding [D24 full-suite attempt]("+failure+") remains a confirmed, unresolved failure: [run `38932318510`](https://github.com/Ginderlax/rea-research-lab/actions/runs/38932318510) executes **1,100 checks: 1,098 pass and two fail**, with no skips, on actual merge `5f23f782a7224aaacdce89edfe21eb7e3a565831` for branch head `d24db806`. The two Archive creation groups refuse native Windows source metadata; their 15,798.2349 ms and 15,590.5217 ms durations align with the 15,000 ms native-child limit. The adapter discarded the original child error and redacted the transport/parse reason, so a timeout is not established. All 798 census bytes and 374 source snapshots match the separately successful `89e00f6` full run byte for byte. Five prerequisite receipts and the independent oracle postcheck passed. Its complete exact public ZIP preserves all 431 uploaded files, both failed TAP blocks and all native metadata sources; 57 nonsource artifact roles are also directly retained. The newer 089c pass does not identify the cause or erase these failures. A separate hosted diagnostic is being prepared to record the native transport outcome under the unchanged command, deadline and test assertions. No runtime correction or reliability acceptance is claimed.\n\n"
"Publication on D24 [run `38932318654`](https://github.com/Ginderlax/rea-research-lab/actions/runs/38932318654) and metadata-only 089c [run `38933603624`](https://github.com/Ginderlax/rea-research-lab/actions/runs/38933603624) passes **208 controls, both root phases and 963 syntax checks**. Both retain 92 readable artifact files plus all 56 decoded Notes-envelope sources. The assessed payload has 28,806 files and 1,364,428,861 bytes; its canonical row identity and publication manifest are equal across the metadata-only transition. Only the two authenticated derived metadata paths were imported at `089cb234`; the automatic repeat's new observation clocks do not require another import. The new failure capsule, diagnostic sources and this documentation form a later payload that requires fresh publication verification. Publication controls execute no application tests and establish no feature or comparative acceptance.\n\n"
"The earlier installed-Notes, Archive and full-suite records below retain their exact source epochs. New To-do's separately accepted 111/8 experimental result is still uninstalled; it is not added to the installed 92 groups, eight browser cases or full-suite total.\n\n"
